--
libc++ (LLVM 18) <tuple>: `std::tuple<int> c(std::forward_as_tuple(3))'
verifies, but CBMC also tries tuple<int>'s element-wise constructor
tuple(_Up &&...) with _Up = tuple<int &&> &, whose
_EnableUTypesCtor<_Up...> constraint (is_constructible<int, tuple<int &&>
&>) should remove it; __tuple_impl's body for it (tuple:469) is dropped.
Not reduced yet; header-free analogues of the deduction and the
constructor's forwarding reference behave (CBMC deduces _Up correctly for
a user-written class).  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and
it fails only its WRONG assertion.
